  "student_passage": "The art room had been closed for a month while workers repaired the ceiling. When the students returned, (1) ____ teacher showed them something nobody had expected. Behind an old noticeboard, the workers had (2) ____ a painting on the wall. It showed children crossing a field towards a small school.\n\nWe were asked not to make any sound while a short film about the painting was being recorded, so everyone moved (3) ____ around the room. Afterwards, our class discussed what should happen to the noticeboard. We had several (4) ____, but covering the painting again was not one of them.\n\nOn the (5) ____ day after the room reopened, we held an afternoon for former pupils. The first eight days had been spent cleaning and arranging chairs. The room looked much more (6) ____ than it had before the repairs, even though we had bought no new paint. We put paper on tables (7) ____ of pinning it to the wall.\n\nSeveral visitors had (8) ____ drawings for school displays many years earlier. They told us how the room used to look. I had expected the afternoon to be dull, but their stories were genuinely (9) ____. When the last visitor left, we (10) ____ put the chairs away. It had been a long day, and I was glad we had left the painting visible for everyone to see.",
