  "filled_passage": "The art room had been closed for a month while workers repaired the ceiling. When the students returned, (1) their teacher showed them something nobody had expected. Behind an old noticeboard, the workers had (2) discovered a painting on the wall. It showed children crossing a field towards a small school.\n\nWe were asked not to make any sound while a short film about the painting was being recorded, so everyone moved (3) silently around the room. Afterwards, our class discussed what should happen to the noticeboard. We had several (4) choices, but covering the painting again was not one of them.\n\nOn the (5) ninth day after the room reopened, we held an afternoon for former pupils. The first eight days had been spent cleaning and arranging chairs. The room looked much more (6) colourful than it had before the repairs, even though we had bought no new paint. We put paper on tables (7) instead of pinning it to the wall.\n\nSeveral visitors had (8) made drawings for school displays many years earlier. They told us how the room used to look. I had expected the afternoon to be dull, but their stories were genuinely (9) interesting. When the last visitor left, we (10) finally put the chairs away. It had been a long day, and I was glad we had left the painting visible for everyone to see.",
